Problem 2
The results show that setting different values for vl and vr is equivalent to "clamping" the beam in different
directions on the left side and on the right side. The intermediate nodes will determine the direction of the
beam in the middle, but the clamps on the end will determine the direction of the beam on the ends.
mesh = linspace(-1.01,1.01,1000);
n = 12;
Xi = linspace(-1,1,n);
Yi = f(Xi);
for i=1:2
    if i == 1
        vl = 5;
        vr = -5;
    else
        vl = -5;
        vr = 5;
    end
    cs = spline(Xi, [vl Yi vr]);
    Ps = ppval(cs, mesh);
    figure();
    plot(Xi, Yi, 'bo');
    hold on;
    plot(mesh, Ps, 'r-');
    hold on;
    plot(mesh, f(mesh), 'k-');
    hold on;
    legend("Nodes", "Splines", "Real Function");
    title("Problem 2 for vl=" + vl + " and vr=" + vr);
end
